<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="prose"><p>Live has no edit. <strong>I'm Sandra Pudja, and I plan and run live productions</strong>: 120+ live productions and 100+ livestreams a year for international video agencies in Berlin and Abu Dhabi, from sports and concerts to international summits, protests and breaking news.</p><p>Daily life was fast decisions. In-house teams, B2B partners and field producers around the world, a schedule that changed by the hour, and a stream that had to go out anyway. I planned the coverage, built the daily and weekly schedules for teams and freelancers, and reported to senior management on risks and resource gaps.</p><p><strong>Clear schedules and clear communication</strong> are what keep a live day calm. That's what I bring to yours.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><h2>What I take care of</h2><div class="grid3"><div class="card"><span class="mono">01</span><h3>Planning</h3><p>Coverage plan, resources, crews and freelancers, aligned with your planning team.</p></div><div class="card"><span class="mono">02</span><h3>Scheduling</h3><p>Daily and weekly schedules for in-house teams, freelancers and field producers.</p></div><div class="card"><span class="mono">03</span><h3>Coordination</h3><p>B2B partners, agencies, venues and technical teams on one plan.</p></div><div class="card"><span class="mono">04</span><h3>Live day</h3><p>Fast decisions, timing and problem solving while it's on air.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><h2>How it works</h2><div class="grid3"><div class="card"><h3>1. Brief</h3><p>What's happening, where, when, and what has to go out.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>2. Plan</h3><p>Schedule, crew, partners and a backup for what could go wrong.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>3. Go live</h3><p>I run the day and keep everyone on the same plan.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><h2>Questions people ask</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What kind of live work have you done?</summary><p>Sports, concerts, cultural events, international summits, protests and breaking news, as livestreams and live productions for international video agencies.</p></details><details><summary>Do you work with in-house teams?</summary><p>Yes. Most of my live work was coordinating in-house teams together with external partners and freelancers.</p></details><details><summary>Can you work internationally?</summary><p>Yes. I've coordinated field producers around the world, and I work in English, German and Croatian.</p></details><details><summary>How early should we book?</summary><p>For planned events, a few weeks ahead is ideal. For fast-moving coverage, get in touch as soon as you know.</p></details></div></div></section>
